\Rightarrow & \frac{d y}{d x}=\frac{2 a}{y}
\end{array}$ Slope of normal $= \left(\frac{-y}{2 a}\right)
At

\left(\mathrm{am}^{2}, 2 \mathrm{am}\right)=\frac{-2 \mathrm{am}}{2 \mathrm{a}}=-\mathrm{m}

Now, the equation of normal to the parabola is

\begin{gathered}
