\mathrm{mx}+\mathrm{y}-\left(2 \mathrm{am}+a \mathrm{ m}^{3}\right)=0 \quad \text{...(i)}
\end{gathered}

Also, given the line

y=m x+c \text{ or } m x-y+c=0 \quad \text{...(ii)}

is normal to parabola, then
On comparing \mathrm{c}=-2  \mathrm{am}-\mathrm{am}^{3}$

